From 530373a2e5345f15343c7c5c6d7e92de7cd4f7c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Segno <noreply@segno.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:44:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm: render Flutter into a multisampled framebuffer and
 resolve it

Impeller's OpenGL ES backend anti-aliases geometry only through 4x
MSAA. The embedder API hands it the backing store's FBO, and the engine
treats that FBO as multisampled only when the context has
GL_EXT_multisampled_render_to_texture
(MakeRenderTargetFromBackingStoreImpeller in embedder.cc). Mesa's V3D
(the Raspberry Pi 5) has GL_MAX_SAMPLES = 4 but not that extension, so
the root pass, which carries every border, rounded rect, circle and
path, reached the screen with no anti-aliasing at all. Offscreen layers
Impeller allocates itself were still multisampled, so the same widget
was smooth under a saveLayer (a colour filter, say) and stair-stepped
without one.

Do what the Windows embedder does on the same kind of driver
(flutter/flutter#190060, cherry-picked as #190374): give each Flutter
backing store a multisampled colour renderbuffer and a multisampled
depth/stencil renderbuffer, hand Flutter that FBO, and resolve it with
glBlitFramebuffer into the active slot at the top of every present,
before any path scans the slot out or composites it. The samples are
then invalidated so a tiler need not write them back. store.fbo becomes
only the resolve target, so its single-sample depth/stencil goes.

Only under Impeller. Skia anti-aliases analytically and wraps the
backing store as single-sample, so a multisampled one would only break
its read-backs (dst reads, backdrop filters) and cost memory.

IVI_DRM_MSAA_SAMPLES sets the sample count (default 4, capped at
GL_MAX_SAMPLES; 0 or 1 turns it off). A store whose multisampled FBO is
incomplete, or whose trial resolve fails (a colour format the driver
will not resolve into), stays single-sample, as before.

Cost at 4x: a 4-sample RGBA8 colour buffer and a 4-sample D24S8 buffer
per backing store, about 66 MB at 1920x1080 and 20 MB at 1024x600, less
the single-sample depth/stencil each store no longer has, plus one
resolve blit per frame per output.

Upstream-Status: Pending
